/-!
# Candidate elementary subgroup representatives and displacement witnesses

The sixty rows specify actual subgroups of the given linear normalizer.
The associated coordinate equations and right inverses are finite data. Their
validity and exhaustive coverage are separate obligations; none is inferred
from the generating program. The ordering agrees with the saved diagnostic: 
code `2*m+e` has upper entries `(01,02,03,12,13,23)` given by the bits of `m`.

Source: Guralnick–Malle, Classification of 2F-modules II, Lemma 4.5 and
Proposition 4.8 step 3A; Aschbacher–Smith K.3.2, printed pp.454–455.
-/

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
@[expose] public section
open Representation Representation.BinaryOffender Matrix
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterK.Linear.Recognition.BinaryCubicSieve.FourDisplacement.Endpoint.FixedBounds

